# One assortative-mating transmission unit at equilibrium:
# a mated pair (m, f) and their two full-sib children (o1, o2).
#
# Assortment is a SINGLE co-path between the partners' phenotypes. That one edge replaces the
# three hand-written induced covariances this file used to carry (g_m<->g_f, e_m<->g_f,
# e_f<->g_m), and it also supplies the one they were missing -- Cov[e_m, e_f] -- so that
# Cov[y_m, y_f] = rho_y * V_P, the defining property of the mating model, now actually holds.
# See examples/am_equilibrium_handwritten.pmg for the superseded encoding and why it was wrong.
#
# The co-path coefficient is NOT the correlation: Cov[y_m, y_f] = mu * V_P^2, so a target
# phenotypic correlation rho_y needs mu = rho_y / V_P. Under assortment V_P grows every
# generation, so mu is generation-indexed -- here it is written out in terms of V_A_eq and V_E
# rather than as a bare symbol, precisely so that dependence stays visible.

units: unstandardized
latent: g_m, e_m, g_f, e_f, g_o1, e_o1, s_o1, g_o2, e_o2, s_o2
positive: V_A_eq, V_E, V_K, V_A0

label: g_m = $g_{m}$
label: e_m = $e_{m}$
label: y_m = $y_{m}$
label: g_f = $g_{f}$
label: e_f = $e_{f}$
label: y_f = $y_{f}$
label: g_o1 = $g_{o1}$
label: e_o1 = $e_{o1}$
label: y_o1 = $y_{o1}$
label: s_o1 = $s_{o1}$
label: g_o2 = $g_{o2}$
label: e_o2 = $e_{o2}$
label: y_o2 = $y_{o2}$
label: s_o2 = $s_{o2}$

# phenotype: y = g + e
y_m  ~ g_m  + e_m
y_f  ~ g_f  + e_f
y_o1 ~ g_o1 + e_o1
y_o2 ~ g_o2 + e_o2

# transmission: g_o = (g_m + g_f)/2 + s_o
g_o1 ~ 1/2*g_m + 1/2*g_f + s_o1
g_o2 ~ 1/2*g_m + 1/2*g_f + s_o2

# the parents are exogenous at the equilibrium scale
g_m ~~ V_A_eq*g_m
g_f ~~ V_A_eq*g_f

e_m  ~~ V_E*e_m
e_f  ~~ V_E*e_f
e_o1 ~~ V_E*e_o1
e_o2 ~~ V_E*e_o2
s_o1 ~~ V_K*s_o1
s_o2 ~~ V_K*s_o2

# assortative mating: one co-path, mu = rho_y / V_P. Every induced covariance among the
# partners' causes -- g with g, e with g, e with e -- follows from this and is NOT written out.
y_m -- (rho_y/(V_A_eq + V_E))*y_f

# the coupled equilibrium fixed point -- to be solved, never traced
assume: rho_g = rho_y*h2_eq
assume: h2_eq = V_A_eq/(V_A_eq + V_E)
assume: V_A_eq = V_A0/(1 - rho_g)
assume: V_K = V_A0/2
